  "text_pages": [
    "Student Housing in Odense\nSkip to main content\nStudents\nitslearning\nAccess to your courses\nmySDU\nFor students at SDU\nSDUmail - Webmail service\nOutlook Web Mail\nSDU Student Self-Service\nCourse registration, exams and results\nLibrary\nSee your status, reservations and renew loans\nDigitalExam\nLogin to DigitalExam\nEmployees\nitslearning\nSDU's e-learn platform\nSDUNet.dk\nSDU's intranet\nDigitalExam\nLogin to DigitalExam\nFind\nFind person\nSearch for contact information on employees\nDirectory\nFinding your way at the University of Southern Denmark\nStudent Housing\nStudent Housing in Odense\nAs an international student in Odense, you are guaranteed housing if you apply on time. Discover your options, find out what to expect, and get practical tips for settling in Denmark’s third largest city.\nOdense offers a wide range of housing options for international students, from residences and housing associations to private rentals and sublets.\nThere are many different housing opportunities in Odense. They differ ind price, location and facilities and is a mix of student residences, private landlords, housing organisations and sublets.\nThe general condition of the housing is reflected in the rent level. Cheaper options are usually older or less modern, but all housing meets acceptable living standards.\nKitchens and bathrooms may be shared, and it cannot be guaranteed that you will only share with students of the same gender.\nAll student housing is furnished with basic items such as a bed, desk, chair and lighting.\nDeadlines\nTo keep your housing guarantee, you must apply before:\n1 May (23:59 CET) for study start in September\n1 November (23:59 CET) for study start in February\nYou can apply for housing even if your application for admission has not yet been accepted.\nApply for housing\nHousing options with SDU agreement\nBelow you will find a list of recommended housing options for international students, where an agreement has been established between the housing provider and SDU.\nCampus House\nSee the facilities and other housing details for Campus House.\nNyborgvej\nRead about the facilities and housing details at this shared apartment.\nToftevej\nRead about the facilities and housing details at these shared apartments.\nHousingOdense\nRead about HousingOdense's approx. 116 student housing options spread across Odense\nDamhusvej\nSee the facilities for this big shared house with 16 private single-rooms.\nNørregade\nSee the facilities at this shared apartment offered by a private landlord.\nØrstedsgade\nRead about the facilities and housing details at this shared apartment.\nSublet\nRead about furnished rooms and apartments subletted for one semester by SDU students.\nDalum Academy\nRead about the facilities at the dormitory. Housing is only optional for autumn semester.\nRasmus Rask Kollegiet\nRead about the facilities and other housing details at the largest student residence in Odense.\nØsterbro 7\nSee the facilities at these shared apartments, with private rooms, shared kitchen and bathroom.\nØsterbro 1\nRead about the facilities and housing details at this modern apartment block.\nH. C. Ørstedskollegiet\nSee the facilities at this student residence with both single rooms and apartments for couples.\nReventlowsvej\nRead about the facilities and housing details at these two shared houses.\nContact\nOdense Office\nCampusvej 1 -\nGround Floor\n5230 Odense M\nOpening hours:\n10 am - 2 pm\nEmail:\nhousing@sdu.dk\nHousing in other campus cities\nEsbjerg\nKolding\nSønderborg\nVejle"
